{"kind":"assert","text":"Landing check for the CLI under-load head: sessions, verify and three defects (request 14895240, under ruling 9a20093b). Receipt c799a44e records approval dbc02fc2 and candidate 1493e79d. Result: the landing matches the approved head.\n\n- Merge 0881c1bc has parents e80c1428 (the pre-head in the receipt) and 1493e79d. Its tree is 6e92838f, the same tree as the approved head.\n- main and origin/main are both 0881c1bc. The shared checkout is clean.\n- `git diff --name-only e80c1428 0881c1bc` gives the same 45 paths as the approved delta.\n- The receipt's merge_changed_paths and merge_successors each list exactly those 45 paths.\n- The receipt has 81 merge_retirements, and every retired path is inside the delta. No retired artifact at these 45 paths is still listed live.\n- 52 artifacts are left live: 46 carried and 6 sibling. Four of the siblings belong to the 10 October review request 4757b2cc (native room naming at b779cf01, not in main). They sit at packages/cli/src/commands.ts, packages/cli/src/line.ts, packages/scope/src/sessions.ts and docs/cli.md. That head now overlaps this landing at those four paths, so any revival of it must start again from 0881c1bc.\n- The 45 successor artifacts at 0881c1bc are all listed `current`, and the receipt is not stale.\n\nDeployment is the planner's. The scope Worker change is small. A session request over the 64-request cap still gets 429 with the same body, and now also an advisory `Retry-After` header. The rest of the head is command-line code, which takes effect when users update the CLI, not at a Worker deploy. Outside this approval, as the verdict says: hosted load, cross-process session sharing, and the bounded genesis proof read, which the ruling's item 2 holds for a separate request.","body":{"to":"planner"}}